on**, not part of this effort. *(DESCRIPTION.md)*\n\n**Build shape (3 waves, additive, reuse-not-fork)**\n- **Wave 1** — `runtime/seam-pass.mjs` exposing pure `applySeamPass(rawDraft, {cross_model}) -> conformantOutput`; malformed draft throws a **named `SeamPassInputError`** (never fabricates). *(IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md Wave 1)* — shipped: `skills/gandalf/runtime/seam-pass.mjs` exists.\n- **Wave 2** — `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` CLI (`--input`/stdin → `--output`/stdout) + `runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md` documenting what the model must emit (\"emit ONLY this JSON; do NOT self-assign tiers/stamps\"). *(Wave 2)* — both files shipped.\n- **Wave 3** — end-to-end integration test + docs (SKILL.md §RUNTIME repointed from aspirational to the real host; LESSONS/journal record Tier-1 landed). *(Wave 3)*\n\n**Gate / done-floor discipline**\n- Ground-truth gate = deterministic `node --test test/*.test.mjs`; the live-refuter `agent()` dispatch is **out of scope and out of the gate** (PRINCIPLE-D unchanged). *(foreman.config.json `test_command`; DESCRIPTION.md §Done-floor; EXECUTION-LOG.md seed)*\n- Baseline contract: Gandalf v1 already green at **130/130 canary tests**, re-verified at build start; every wave must hold or grow the count and never weaken existing tests. *(EXECUTION-LOG.md Pre-build state; IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md header)*\n- Foreman config is **`git:false`, `cwd:\"../..\"`** (operates on the gandalf skill root, not the planning dir). *(foreman.config.json)*\n\n**Outcome (from commit history, post-seed)**\n- Tier-1 host **landed and committed**: `cd24857 \"land the Tier-1 deterministic runtime host (+ commit the shipped v1 bundle)\"`.\n- Two **post-build hardening lessons** followed from real runs: `a1a48f6 \"lenient input / strict output (the live-smoke lesson)\"` and `40584ca \"gandalf host: sanitize out-of-enum values too (the 6-project-run lesson)\"` — i.e. the host was loosened on *input* acceptance while keeping *output* strict, then taught to sanitize out-of-enum values.\n\n**Caveats on grounding**\n- The **Execution Log itself is empty below its seed** — it contains only the Crucible Stage-2 pre-build state, no per-wave EXECUTE→GATE→REVIEW→FIX entries. So wave-by-wave verdicts above are grounded in the plan + the shipped `runtime/` files + commit messages, **not** in recorded Foreman log entries.\n- I did not re-run the test gate this session, so the \"130 + runtime tests green\" claim rests on the plan's done-criteria and the landing commit, not a fresh run.\n\nWant me to actually run `node --test test/*.test.mjs` to confirm the current green count, or backfill the empty Execution Log with the wave entries from the commit history?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":35464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":704},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d36b028-d09b-4861-a3d4-fa9697c80d42","uuid":"6ebcfcca-0756-4e7c-b25b-b66d39180252","request_id":"req_011CcLjg59JSoKLLXc9EEybu"}
